    pr_ref:  # f5a4
    description: "## Problem\n\nTracker discussion threads are append-only with no way to delete or edit a specific past message. Existing options operate on the whole thread (`discuss --clear` wipes everything; `discuss --summarize` replaces everything with a single entry). Both are human-only. There is no surgical \"remove this one entry\" operation.\n\nThis makes fold-correction workflows harder than they should be. The 2026-06-03 fold-audit identified ~56 reconstructed-row proposals that exist as discussion-entry text on parent rows (INV-luhur, INV-virik, INV-numat, INV-napap, INV-titid, INV-bikaj, INV-bazij, WI-bupim) and should be extracted into their own discrete rows. Without per-message delete/edit, the materialization workflow is additive-only (file new rows, leave the parent discussion bloated forever) — functionally fine but it leaves the over-fold record permanently in the way of routine reading.\n\n## Solution sketch\n\nAdd three new tracker ops — `delete-msg`, `undelete-msg`, `edit-msg-text` — gated behind a time-boxed, human-authorized \"edit-mode\" window. All ops are append-only (tombstones / supersessions, not destructive). OS-level permissions enforce the gate: only the human user can enable edit-mode; the agent can write the message ops at any time but they're filtered at compile if not bracketed by a valid edit-mode-on window.\n\n## Design decisions (interview, 2026-06-03)\n\n| # | Decision | Choice |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Message identity | Built-in 4-char `nonce` (already on every op; no migration) |\n| 2 | Edit-mode scope | `delete-msg` + `undelete-msg` + `edit-msg-text` only |\n| 3 | Auth model | Window-based; OS-perm via 2-user model |\n| 4 | Toggle UI | CLI subcommand + TUI keybind; both write `edit-mode-on` op |\n| 5 | TTL | `--ttl` flag, default 30 min, max 60 min, half-open `[start, start+ttl)` |\n| 6 | Op cap | 500 successful `delete-msg`+`edit-msg-text` per window; undelete free; failed ops free |\n| 7 | Reason field | Required, free-text, ≤100 chars |\n| 8 | Show output | Hidden by default; terse footer `(not shown: N deleted messages)` only when N>0; no flag hint in footer |\n| 9 | Agent status check | Implicit — try-and-fail with clear error (no status subcommand surfaced to agent) |\n| 10 | `edit-msg-text` semantics | Supersede in place; preserve nonce; chain unlimited edits; latest text wins |\n| 11 | Edit on tombstoned message | Reject; must undelete first |\n| 12 | Manual off | Yes — CLI + TUI both write `edit-mode-off` op |\n| 13 | Overlapping windows | Replace — new `on` op starts fresh window |\n\n## Op shapes\n\n```yaml\n# edit-mode-on (written by human user; rejected by OS perm if not human)\n- op: edit-mode-on\n  at: 2026-06-03T00:30:00.000Z\n  by: human\n  user_id: jgstern\n  ttl_seconds: 1800   # default 30m, --ttl flag, max 3600\n  cap_max: 500\n  nonce: a3f2\n\n# edit-mode-off (also human-only)\n- op: edit-mode-off\n  at: 2026-06-03T00:35:00.000Z\n  by: human\n  user_id: jgstern\n  nonce: b7c4\n\n# delete-msg (agent-issuable when window is open)\n- op: delete-msg\n  at: 2026-06-03T00:31:14.142Z\n  by: agent\n  user_id: jgstern-agent\n  item: INV-luhur-sital-...\n  target_nonce: a3f2\n  reason: \"extracted to WI-compact-truncation-marker\"  # required, <=100 chars\n  nonce: c8d1\n\n# undelete-msg (same shape; not cap-counted)\n- op: undelete-msg\n  at: ...\n  by: agent\n  user_id: jgstern-agent\n  item: INV-luhur-...\n  target_nonce: a3f2\n  reason: \"reverting; the WI-extraction was wrong\"\n  nonce: d4e5\n\n# edit-msg-text (cap-counted)\n- op: edit-msg-text\n  at: ...\n  by: agent\n  user_id: jgstern-agent\n  item: INV-luhur-...\n  target_nonce: a3f2\n  new_text: \"Pass-40 F40.A1+A2+A3 batch (corrected wording)...\"\n  reason: \"wording fix\"\n  nonce: e6f7\n```\n\n## Compile rules\n\n1. **Edit-mode windows.** Walk all `edit-mode-on` and `edit-mode-off` ops in chronological order. Each `edit-mode-on` opens a window `[at, at + ttl_seconds)`. The next `edit-mode-off` (or new `edit-mode-on`) terminates the previous window at its `at`. The window also auto-terminates at `at + ttl_seconds` if neither event happens first.\n\n2. **Op authorization.** For each `delete-msg` / `undelete-msg` / `edit-msg-text` op, check that its `at` falls within at least one OS-verified `edit-mode-on` window (i.e., the `edit-mode-on` op was written by `by:human` AND the file system attests it was written by the human-user). If not, the op is filtered (ignored at compile, NOT removed from `.ops`).\n\n3. **Cap enforcement.** Within each window, count valid `delete-msg` + `edit-msg-text` ops (NOT `undelete-msg`, NOT failed/filtered). If a window contains more than `cap_max=500`, ignore the (cap_max+1)-th and beyond.\n\n4. **Message rendering.** For each `discuss` op (existing), walk subsequent ops in the same item's `.ops` file:\n   - If any `delete-msg` references this nonce (and is not later overridden by `undelete-msg`), mark message as tombstoned.\n   - If any `edit-msg-text` references this nonce, replace text with the LATEST edit's `new_text`.\n   - If both: edit-then-delete shows latest text under tombstone; edit-on-tombstoned should not exist (rejected at write time).\n\n5. **Default show output.** Suppress tombstoned messages. If any tombstones exist for the item, append a single line: `(not shown: N deleted messages)`. No flag hint. The `--include-deleted` flag (documented in `tracker show --help` only) renders tombstones with strikethrough/dim plus their delete reason+by+at. `--include-history` (documented in `--help` only) renders edit chains for each message.\n\n## OS permission model\n\n- Create `.agent/tracker/.edit_mode_ops/` owned by human user (mode 0755): agent has read access, no write access.\n- `tracker edit-mode on` / `off` CLI and TUI keybind both write into this directory. They MUST be run as the human user; agent-user invocations fail with permission error.\n- Compile rule: an `edit-mode-on` op is valid only if its containing `.ops` file (or directory entry) attests human ownership at the OS layer. This prevents agent forgery via direct YAML manipulation.\n- Setup script (or `tracker init --with-edit-mode`) creates the directory with correct ownership at repo init time.\n\n## Agent CLI surface\n\n```\ntracker delete-msg <item> <nonce> --reason \"<text ≤100 chars>\"\ntracker undelete-msg <item> <nonce> --reason \"<text ≤100 chars>\"\ntracker edit-msg-text <item> <nonce> --new-text \"<text>\" --reason \"<text ≤100 chars>\"\n```\n\nAll three return `rc=1` with a clear error when edit-mode is off:\n```\nEdit-mode is not active. This op cannot be applied. (Human can run \"tracker edit-mode on\" to enable.)\n```\n\nNo `tracker edit-mode status` subcommand is surfaced for the agent (implicit-check principle).\n\n## Human CLI / TUI surface\n\n```\ntracker edit-mode on [--ttl <duration>]   # default 30m, max 60m\ntracker edit-mode off                      # close window early\ntracker edit-mode status                   # show {on, remaining_s, ops_used/cap_max} — human-facing\n```\n\nTUI: dedicated keybind (e.g., Ctrl-E) toggles edit-mode. While on, banner at top: `EDIT MODE ON — 24m remaining — 12/500 ops used`.\n\n## Backward compatibility\n\n- All existing discuss ops already carry nonces (`_make_nonce()` at `store.py:177`); no migration needed.\n- No existing `edit-mode-on` ops in any `.ops` file → no agent-issued `delete-msg`/`edit-msg-text` ops from before this feature shipped would be honored even if hand-crafted.\n- `tracker show` output before this feature has no `(not shown: N deleted)` footer; after this feature, the footer appears only when N>0.\n\n## Out of scope for v1\n\n- Manifest-based authorization (`tracker apply-manifest`) — considered, not chosen\n- Edit history on messages by default (forensic mode only via `--include-history`)\n- Per-message permissions / per-author restrictions\n- Status-field overrides during edit-mode\n- Bulk operations (e.g., `delete-msg --item X --before <date>`)\n\n## Companion artifacts\n\n- 2026-06-03 fold-audit: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md` — the audit that surfaced the need for this feature.\n- 2026-06-03 design interview: this WI's design table reflects choices made interactively with josh@iterabloom.com.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Touches `.agent/tracker/**` and possibly `scripts/tracker` and `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/`. **Governance files: human approval required for the implementation PR.** Do NOT self-merge.\n- Implementation order suggested:\n  1. Add op-type schemas + compile rules (no UI changes yet)\n  2. Add OS-perm scaffolding + `edit-mode-on`/`off` CLI for human\n  3. Add agent CLI for `delete-msg`/`undelete-msg`/`edit-msg-text`\n  4. Update `tracker show` rendering (default + `--include-deleted` + `--include-history`)\n  5. TUI keybind + banner\n  6. Self-test: materialize one of the 56 fold-audit proposals end-to-end as a smoke test"  # f5a4
    fields: {}  # f5a4
